# The JARVIS theme (Stark's heads-up display): picked in Settings > Appearance, its feature names (the command palette is
# JARVIS, review is "Awaiting your approval"), its sounds named in Settings, and the Environment panel in it, which lists
# every program (SPARTA with the optional packages its build lacks). Then back to LCARS.
open $SB/ws/cavity
# the GPU query (nvidia-smi, once a session, ~100 ms) is not what this measures: open the panel once first
click env-status
wait-until modal environment timeout 5
key ESCAPE
wait 3
measure
click nav:settings
wait-until page Settings timeout 5
wait 5
click label:JARVIS
wait 5
assert text Awaiting your approval
assert text Soft holographic ticks
screenshot $OUT/jarvis_settings.png
click nav:overview
wait-until page Overview
click env-status
wait-until modal environment timeout 5
assert text SPARTA
assert text Rarefied gas
assert text Chrono
assert text JARVIS sounds
screenshot $OUT/jarvis_env.png
# spa_mpi -h is read in the background (a second: MPI starts); the panel fills it in when it arrives
wait-until text without the optional packages timeout 15
key ESCAPE
wait 3
key K ctrl
wait-until modal palette timeout 5
assert text JARVIS
key ESCAPE
wait 3
theme 0
wait 5
assert modal none
budget p95 16.7 max 100
